    "interpretation": "The auto_log tier contains flows the prioritizer routed to routine handling. B4's key honest question is: of those, how many were real attacks / zero-days, and what did the detector believe about them? If the auto-logged attacks all have predicted_label='normal', high confidence, and below-threshold reconstruction error, then the auto-logging is a downstream consequence of a detection failure (the hybrid confidently misclassified the attack as normal on both signals), not a prioritizer error. If instead the auto-logged attacks had anomalous recon or a confident known-family label, that would indicate a prioritizer routing problem. The cross_tab_* fields make this distinction checkable. This audit reports counts; it does NOT assert that auto-logging is safe. Whether the residual is acceptable is an operational decision."
